1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
This is IronVision AI: human-approved AI for the NIST Risk Management Framework.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:13,000
Everything here runs in a shared demonstration workspace with synthetic data, one click from sign-in.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:20,000
Personas let one presenter act as ISSO, assessor and AO, and every action stays labelled.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The RMF overview is the command center: all seven NIST 800-37 steps, computed from live records, with the criteria behind every status.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Ongoing work and the single next action are always one click away.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:45,000
As the ISSM, the portfolio shows authorizations, CAT I and KEV exposure, overdue POA&Ms, and what is waiting on you.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Prepare and Categorize start at registration: name the system, assign the RMF key roles, and answer whether it is a National Security System.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Step one tracks every required role. Here, the assessor is still missing.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Federal systems use FIPS 199: information types roll up to a high-water mark.

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:16,000
For a national security system, CNSSI 1253 keeps confidentiality, integrity and availability separate, and prompts for the Privacy Overlay.

11
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Integrity was raised to High with a recorded rationale, and the change waited for the AO's approval before it took effect.

12
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:35,000
Select then applies the CNSSI 1253 baseline: five hundred fifty-nine controls, each traced to its source table, plus overlays, tailoring and parameters.

13
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:47,500
Implementation happens in the Control Workbench. For AC-2, the ISSO sees status, supporting evidence with hashes and freshness, open findings and mapped policies in one place.

14
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:58,000
AI can draft the statement, grounded in that evidence with validated citations. It is labelled as AI and never auto-approved.

15
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:20,000
Mapping Review puts the control requirement next to the exact policy passage. Automated matching and AI only propose; a person accepts, rejects or overrides with a justification. Nothing changes a compliance record until a human decides.

16
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Evidence arrives as STIG, SCAP, ACAS or Nessus files. Live connectors here are mocked.

17
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Each ingest run is hashed, deduplicated and mapped through CCIs to NIST 800-53 controls, including this Log4j finding from an ACAS scan.

18
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:49,000
Test Results imports the eMASS Test Result template and is designed to preserve it. Rows are proposed from assessments, scans and evidence; AI explains each row.

19
00:02:49,500 --> 00:03:05,000
Only the Security Control Assessor approves a result, and must record who actually tested and when. AI never sets compliance status, tester or test date.

20
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:16,000
The authorization package brings together the SSP, assessment results, POA&Ms and risk acceptances, with OSCAL exports. The ISSO can submit it, but the decision is AO-only.

21
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:24,000
POA&Ms rank risk, flag KEV and CAT I items, and show sync status with a mocked eMASS connector.

22
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:45,000
After ISSM endorsement, the Authorizing Official records the decision: ATO, ATO with conditions, IATT or denial, with rationale and expiration. Separation of duties is enforced; no one approves their own work, and in a real organization that means a different person.

23
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Continuous monitoring watches evidence freshness, CAT I findings, CISA KEV and overdue POA&Ms.

24
00:03:53,000 --> 00:04:00,000
The Evidence Ledger keeps every artifact with its SHA-256 hash, provenance and versions.

25
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:05,500
Traceability links each control to evidence, findings, POA&Ms and assessment.

26
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:25,000
And every action, including each review and approval, lands in a hash-chained, append-only audit log you can verify and export.

27
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:33,000
From preparation to continuous monitoring, the whole lifecycle stays in one place.

28
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:46,000
IronVision AI: human-approved AI for the NIST Risk Management Framework. AI does the heavy lifting; people keep the authority.

29
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:56,000
Get audit-ready, and stay audit-ready. Request your demo today.
